[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-7598"] :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=4$ and ${b}^{2}=16.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=4,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{4}=2.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=16,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{16}=4.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $b=4,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=2.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 4=8,$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 2=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-69893"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041013/assets/be8468d84e3820bd1e9181d31aa3a1b7d1a85c743020a69cb67fc3f601a88363.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-115129"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041013/assets/c71a52cc148f8ce4a23a2fb2005757c9d141d3caf05586d8fb5122f591dc7474.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-279165/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "33472bbc-2958-5b76-9fd7-e4be00b37d70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-279165/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "51a28714-a125-53b7-8a56-9d8e5eb5fd8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-279165/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "de0b8d34-f76b-543f-ad36-2d004571145a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-279165/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer-field/choices ["q-279165/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-279165/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-279165/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "bc2e44ce-3a5b-51df-aea3-bff0213280ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-279165/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "8274bf2f-e625-59e7-8f11-4a513638b6af" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-279165/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-279165/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-279165" :question/id #uuid "1f865070-f5b3-5500-a742-b83f4ec5d86b" :question/math-academy-id "q-279165" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=9$ and ${b}^{2}=4.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=9,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{9}=3.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=4,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{4}=2.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $a=3,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=2.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 3=6,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 2=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-279165/field-1" "q-279165/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-279165"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-279166/field-1/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "4aaeb91a-64e6-5fec-8909-27232704b53b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-279166/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "93b4a93e-f7aa-53d4-8e4f-f1ff1353c830" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-279166/field-1/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer-field/choices ["q-279166/field-1/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-279166/field-2/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "8cc8fa3e-a39d-560c-adf0-fe9d14532ffa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-279166/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "61154251-8d8a-58c7-b516-d8b455260b49" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-279166/field-2/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer-field/choices ["q-279166/field-2/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-279166" :question/id #uuid "a7f34816-fae1-5bab-b494-08ab8f5462c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-279166" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=36$ and ${b}^{2}=16.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=36,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{36}=6.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=16,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{16}=4.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $a=6,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=4.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 6=12,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 4=8.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-279166/field-1" "q-279166/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-279166"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
